From e3a871785878b25b916cd8f50cd59b07ea5cd57a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 215/240] Bugfix: require the CMake version that the build
 files need [report R. Perry]

The CMake files declared a minimum version of 3.10, but use the
NAME_WLE mode of `get_filename_component()` (CMake 3.14), the
LibLZMA::LibLZMA imported target (3.14) and `cmake -E cat` (3.18), so
that configuration or testing failed with CMake 3.10 to 3.17 although
the documentation promised otherwise.

Require CMake 3.18 and update the documentation accordingly.

Refs: BLD-13
---
 CMakeLists.txt          | 2 +-
 README.md               | 2 +-
 doc/src/handson/h_c.tex | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index b4434ec..dfc2a68 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 ##                                                        ##
 ############################################################
 
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)
 
 project(SCOTCH LANGUAGES C)
 
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6a292dd..ee6a3bf 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@ Installation
 
 Two flavors of installation are available:
 
-* With CMake, using version 3.10 or higher:
+* With CMake, using version 3.18 or higher:
 
 ```bash
 mkdir build && cd build && cmake .. && make -j5
diff --git a/doc/src/handson/h_c.tex b/doc/src/handson/h_c.tex
index 0acdf84..a16b71c 100644
--- a/doc/src/handson/h_c.tex
+++ b/doc/src/handson/h_c.tex
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ In order to compile \scotch, one needs:
 \item
   GNU make;
 \item
-  possibly CMake, version at least~3.10;
+  possibly CMake, version at least~3.18;
 \item
   a C compiler that can handle the C99 standard (and is parametrized
   to do so);
